  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New York has recorded $10.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 16.5% year over year, and federal buyers issued 289,569 awards with an average award size of $34.8K. Fiscal-year comparisons show a multi-year decline from $30.8B in FY21 to $10.1B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $5B in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the single largest industry category at $842M. BROOKHAVEN SCIENCE ASSOCIATES LLC is the top vendor with $842M in awards. Other sizable buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $916M, the Department of Energy at $909M, and the General Services Administration at $753M. Multiple NAICS categories are at or above $309M, including Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $816M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $701M. The figures reported are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
