        "heading": "How has federal contracting in New York changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 16.5% year over year. New York obligations fell from $30.8B in FY21 to $10.1B in FY26. Award volume remains large at 289,569 awards, and the average award size is $34.8K. The fiscal totals for FY26 are partial and represent the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal spending in New York?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5B, making it the largest buyer in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $916M and the Department of Energy obligated $909M. BROOKHAVEN SCIENCE ASSOCIATES LLC received $842M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears with awards of $586M and $369M on the vendor list."
      }
